Reveal ladder

Use the current architecture, but preserve this general order:

Something remains after correction.

The surviving shape can appear outside its original case.

Preserved contradictions can become usable routes.

Different people and systems respond according to their remaining relationships.

B’s own memory has been corrected.

Severed provenance produces ownerless pressure.

Ownerless pressure follows affinity and acquires carriers.

Repeated correction changes what survives.

Noor may persist within the resulting ecology without being reducible to it.

Recognition does not create a right to restoration or ownership.

Do not treat this list as fixed chapter numbering. Audit against the newest architecture.

Tone checks

A line belongs when it does at least one of the following:

Reveals character

Makes the institution physically or socially legible

Changes the pressure of the scene

Deepens the image or emotional consequence

Creates dry humor from how people survive the system

A line is suspect when it exists mainly to sound clever, profound, or quotable.